From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:45:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: mark messages and replies on the pane scrollbar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pane.mark.list lists the messages in a pane's scrollback with the row
each starts on. For Claude Code they are read from the scrollback as
printed: a "❯" line after a blank row is one of the user's messages,
and a "●" line in the colour of that text is one of its replies (a
tool call's is coloured by how the call went). That covers a resumed
session's history, and previous_input/next_input stop at the same
messages. Other agents list the messages the server marked.

The client asks for a shown agent pane's list when its agent changes
state, when the pane changes width, and when the scrollback of an
agent that isn't working changes length. It draws a mark in the
scrollbar column on the row the thumb's top moves to when the view
shows the message or reply. Hovering a mark lists what is on its row
in a card; clicking one outside the thumb scrolls it one row below
the top.

A mark only counts as a message while it is still on the screen when
the agent starts working: a resumed session printed its history over
the mark made at startup, which then passed for the first message.

